==Trivia==
*The word "''Skeleton''" comes from the Greek "''σκελετός''" (''skeletós''), meaning dried up or withered.
**The Skeletons are 1 of 6 evolved [[cards]] associated with [[Skeletons]], with the others being [[Bomber/Evolution|Bomber]], [[Skeleton Barrel/Evolution|Skeleton Barrel]], [[Witch/Evolution|Witch]], [[Wall Breakers/Evolution|Wall Breakers]], and [[Skeleton Army/Evolution|Skeleton Army]].
*The beginning of the Skeletons' Evolution description, "When there's no room in Spooky Town, the dead will walk the Arena!", references the famous quote, "When there's no more room in Hell, the dead will walk the Earth." from Dawn of the Dead.
*The Skeletons' Evolution is tied with the [[Ice Spirit/Evolution|Ice Spirit]] for the cheapest [[Card Evolution|Evolution]] to be placed, costing 3 [[Elixir]] (excluding Elixir from using other cards).
*The Skeletons' Evolution was one of the first Evolutions to be added in the game, alongside the [[Barbarians/Evolution|Barbarians]], [[Royal Giant/Evolution|Royal Giant]], and [[Firecracker/Evolution|Firecracker]]. It is also one of the first evolved [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] to be featured in a [[Loading Screens|Loading Screen]], alongside the Barbarians, Royal Giant, and Firecracker.
*The Skeletons' Evolution is 1 of 5 [[cards]] that has had its Cycles required changed, the others being [[Bomber/Evolution|Bomber]], Ice Spirit, [[Lumberjack/Evolution|Lumberjack]], and [[Baby Dragon/Evolution|Baby Dragon]].
*Even though the card spawns 3 Skeletons, the card render displays only 1 Skeleton.
*The Skeletons' Evolution are 1 of 5 evolved troops which can defeat themselves in one attack, the others being Firecracker, [[Wall Breakers/Evolution|Wall Breakers]], Runners, and [[Goblin Barrel/Evolution|Decoy Goblins]].
*The Skeletons' Evolution are the only evolved swarm card whose members spawn all at the exact same time.
*In the Korean language settings of the game, the Skeletons' name translates to "Skeleton Soldiers".
*The Skeletons' Evolution is the subject of an [[Emotes|Emote]].
*Before the Skeletons' Evolution's release, the cycles required was increased to 3 (from 2), and the maximum number of Evolved Skeletons was decreased to 6 (from 8).

